1
00:00:15,025 --> 00:00:16,264
You hit me this hard.

2
00:00:16,265 --> 00:00:17,625
You really hate me that much, huh?

3
00:00:18,105 --> 00:00:19,865
I just asked what you two are to each other.

4
00:00:21,505 --> 00:00:22,505
Oh,

5
00:00:23,745 --> 00:00:25,185
so you like him, huh?

6
00:00:25,985 --> 00:00:27,265
You can think whatever you want.

7
00:00:28,465 --> 00:00:31,025
But if you cause Comrade Saeng any trouble,

8
00:00:32,065 --> 00:00:33,265
I won't hold back like today.

9
00:00:37,385 --> 00:00:38,385
Hmph.

10
00:00:39,465 --> 00:00:40,945
Ouch! Ouch!

11
00:00:44,865 --> 00:00:46,705
Whatever you want or dream of becoming,

12
00:00:48,105 --> 00:00:49,905
I’ll make sure none of it comes true.

13
00:02:20,545 --> 00:02:23,105
Lately, we’ve been taking care of each other’s wounds.

14
00:02:35,585 --> 00:02:37,905
Comrade Fah knows about us, right?

15
00:02:46,865 --> 00:02:49,025
As long as I’m here, you don’t have to be afraid, Vin.

16
00:02:51,665 --> 00:02:52,665
I know.

17
00:02:53,265 --> 00:02:55,384
But when Comrade Fah gets angry,

18
00:02:55,385 --> 00:02:56,905
he’s not someone easy to stop.

19
00:02:58,145 --> 00:02:59,345
Look at Comrade Bai Tong.

20
00:03:00,025 --> 00:03:01,705
No one even knows how she’s doing now.

21
00:03:04,025 --> 00:03:05,745
Comrade Baitong is with Comrade Ying now.

22
00:03:06,505 --> 00:03:07,505
She's fine.

23
00:03:18,825 --> 00:03:20,145
Why are you burning up like this?

24
00:03:21,305 --> 00:03:22,585
Do you have a fever?

25
00:03:24,905 --> 00:03:25,905
Comrade.

26
00:03:26,305 --> 00:03:27,825
Have you seen Comrade Bai Tong?

27
00:03:32,385 --> 00:03:33,385
Bai Tong!

28
00:03:34,105 --> 00:03:35,105
Bai Tong!

29
00:03:35,985 --> 00:03:36,985
Bai Tong!

30
00:03:42,145 --> 00:03:43,145
Bai Tong!

31
00:03:44,665 --> 00:03:45,665
Bai Tong!

32
00:03:48,345 --> 00:03:49,345
Bai Tong!

33
00:03:52,385 --> 00:03:53,385
Bai Tong!

34
00:03:54,625 --> 00:03:55,625
Bai Tong!

35
00:04:03,305 --> 00:04:05,184
You two, move everything out.

36
00:04:05,185 --> 00:04:06,705
Don’t leave a single piece behind. Go!

37
00:04:07,185 --> 00:04:08,705
Don’t take my father’s things!

38
00:04:09,185 --> 00:04:10,305
- Hey!
- Don’t!

39
00:04:10,985 --> 00:04:12,785
- Bai Tong.
- Don’t take my father’s things!

40
00:04:20,945 --> 00:04:22,064
Wearing makeup and fixing your hair like-

41
00:04:22,065 --> 00:04:23,705
-this is against Party rules, understand?

42
00:04:40,465 --> 00:04:41,305
Did you find her?

43
00:04:41,305 --> 00:04:42,305
No, not at all.

44
00:05:02,105 --> 00:05:03,105
Bai Tong.

45
00:05:05,625 --> 00:05:06,785
Bai Tong, it’s me.

46
00:05:08,705 --> 00:05:09,705
Bai Tong.

47
00:05:15,585 --> 00:05:16,585
Bai Tong.

48
00:05:18,025 --> 00:05:19,025
Bai Tong, it’s me.

49
00:05:26,065 --> 00:05:27,065
I’m here now.

50
00:05:28,185 --> 00:05:29,185
I promise.

51
00:05:29,665 --> 00:05:31,705
I won’t let anyone hurt you again.

52
00:05:33,745 --> 00:05:35,025
Let’s go back to our base.

53
00:05:36,785 --> 00:05:38,305
It’s okay now.

54
00:06:01,265 --> 00:06:02,265
Yaguar.

55
00:06:06,145 --> 00:06:07,945
How is Comrade Baitong doing?

56
00:06:10,905 --> 00:06:12,905
She cried so much she got a fever.

57
00:06:14,545 --> 00:06:15,745
I just sponged her down.

58
00:06:53,985 --> 00:06:55,865
Why is Comrade Ying crying?

59
00:07:05,305 --> 00:07:07,064
Comrade Bai Tong.

60
00:07:07,065 --> 00:07:09,345
Keeps crying and calling for Comrade Ploeng in her sleep.

61
00:07:09,985 --> 00:07:12,145
She keeps crying and apologizing to Comrade Fah.

62
00:07:15,145 --> 00:07:18,185
How can a leader like this make the country better?

63
00:07:26,505 --> 00:07:28,425
I want to help Bai Tong escape from the forest.

64
00:07:32,105 --> 00:07:34,305
I don’t want to stay here anymore.

65
00:07:36,665 --> 00:07:37,865
Are you serious, Comrade Ying?

66
00:07:41,105 --> 00:07:42,705
I don’t want to stay here anymore.

67
00:07:43,865 --> 00:07:44,865
If you really mean it,

68
00:07:46,425 --> 00:07:47,785
I’ll find a way to help.

69
00:07:54,545 --> 00:07:56,265
Please help us, Yaguar.

70
00:07:57,705 --> 00:07:58,945
Please don’t cry, okay?

71
00:08:38,665 --> 00:08:39,105
Sir.

72
00:08:39,505 --> 00:08:40,505
Hey, sir.

73
00:08:42,265 --> 00:08:43,265
Yaguar.

74
00:08:44,225 --> 00:08:46,305
You called me here so suddenly. Is something wrong?

75
00:08:46,705 --> 00:08:48,185
Can you help take me somewhere else?

76
00:08:50,465 --> 00:08:51,625
Are people suspicious of you?

77
00:08:52,945 --> 00:08:53,945
No.

78
00:08:55,545 --> 00:08:57,105
I just don’t want to stay here anymore.

79
00:08:57,865 --> 00:08:59,625
Three or four people are coming with me too.

80
00:08:59,985 --> 00:09:00,985
Can you help them too?

81
00:09:03,385 --> 00:09:04,825
Did something happen in there?

82
00:09:10,385 --> 00:09:12,465
Comrade Fah has been promoted to leader of the base.

83
00:09:13,385 --> 00:09:15,105
But he ended up hurting Pleong's daughter.

84
00:09:21,545 --> 00:09:22,545
Tonight at 2AM,

85
00:09:22,985 --> 00:09:25,305
I’ll wait near the exit by the old shooting range.

86
00:09:30,305 --> 00:09:32,105
But you have to help me with something first.

87
00:09:38,865 --> 00:09:41,584
The other day, I took May back to the Baan Kop Ku.

88
00:09:41,585 --> 00:09:44,185
I heard someone from the main base is coming to inspect our base.

89
00:09:45,745 --> 00:09:47,784
If they’re coming without prior notice,

90
00:09:47,785 --> 00:09:49,425
it’s probably not a normal inspection.

91
00:09:50,225 --> 00:09:52,464
I think it’s an order from the main base.

92
00:09:52,465 --> 00:09:54,304
To clean up the problems in our base.

93
00:09:54,305 --> 00:09:57,945
Right. Our leader died because of a traitor.

94
00:09:58,785 --> 00:10:00,904
And the people in our base are mentally falling apart.

95
00:10:00,905 --> 00:10:02,025
Because of Comrade Bai Tong.

96
00:10:02,425 --> 00:10:04,704
If the inspection finds issues at our base,

97
00:10:04,705 --> 00:10:06,944
they might even replace the leader.

98
00:10:06,945 --> 00:10:08,785
What exactly are you trying to say, Phu pha?

99
00:10:11,145 --> 00:10:13,585
The biggest problem right now is the traitor inside our base.

100
00:10:14,745 --> 00:10:16,664
If we find out first,

101
00:10:16,665 --> 00:10:18,744
We just report the main base that it’s been resolved.

102
00:10:18,745 --> 00:10:19,745
We will.

103
00:10:19,905 --> 00:10:20,905
We have to.

104
00:10:21,025 --> 00:10:23,544
Alive or dead, I don’t care anymore.

105
00:10:23,545 --> 00:10:24,745
Comrade Fah.

106
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:29,384
Yakwa arranged for that Thai soldier-

107
00:10:29,385 --> 00:10:31,065
-to help our people escape tonight.

108
00:10:33,585 --> 00:10:34,585
I told you.

109
00:10:34,985 --> 00:10:36,505
He is a traitor.

110
00:10:40,705 --> 00:10:41,825
Damn it.

111
00:11:04,425 --> 00:11:05,425
Vin.

112
00:11:17,025 --> 00:11:18,785
Didn’t you already take your medicine?

113
00:11:19,225 --> 00:11:20,665
Why hasn’t your fever gone down yet?

114
00:11:23,505 --> 00:11:25,185
We’re running low on medicine at the base,

115
00:11:25,825 --> 00:11:27,305
So I only took one dose.

116
00:11:29,745 --> 00:11:31,025
Maybe some rest will help.

117
00:11:32,625 --> 00:11:34,425
How will you get better on and off your meds?

118
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:39,505
I’ll go get more medicine.

119
00:11:55,265 --> 00:11:58,625
(My son, my little sun)

120
00:12:15,545 --> 00:12:21,865
(Meet me at Chan Siao Cave tonight.)
(Brother)

121
00:13:21,105 --> 00:13:22,105
Vin.

122
00:13:27,945 --> 00:13:29,265
Why do you look so pale?

123
00:13:30,145 --> 00:13:31,185
Are you sick?

124
00:13:32,145 --> 00:13:33,305
Why did you ask me to come?

125
00:13:33,985 --> 00:13:35,185
I can’t stay long.

126
00:13:41,745 --> 00:13:42,905
From Aunt Laor.

127
00:13:43,625 --> 00:13:45,105
She said she misses you much.

128
00:13:49,025 --> 00:13:51,425
Tell my mom I miss her too.

129
00:13:52,465 --> 00:13:53,665
Very much.

130
00:13:58,425 --> 00:13:59,425
I...

131
00:14:01,425 --> 00:14:02,945
I... miss you too, Vin.

132
00:14:10,585 --> 00:14:13,225
"Ever since I moved away and went to military prep school,

133
00:14:13,945 --> 00:14:17,145
"I finally realized that I never saw you as just...

134
00:14:21,025 --> 00:14:22,025
a younger brother.

135
00:14:34,185 --> 00:14:35,665
You mean more to me than that.

136
00:14:54,825 --> 00:14:56,785
But I only see you as my older brother.

137
00:15:14,745 --> 00:15:16,704
Yeah. I guess I rushed things.

138
00:15:16,705 --> 00:15:18,385
Saying something like this out of nowhere.

139
00:15:19,505 --> 00:15:20,505
Well,

140
00:15:20,905 --> 00:15:22,265
Forget what I said for now.

141
00:15:23,065 --> 00:15:25,585
Just think about whether you want to go home and see Aunt Laor.

142
00:15:26,185 --> 00:15:27,185
That’s enough.

143
00:15:28,225 --> 00:15:29,385
If you want to,

144
00:15:29,985 --> 00:15:30,985
I know a way.

145
00:16:25,025 --> 00:16:26,625
Didn’t I tell you already?

146
00:16:27,225 --> 00:16:28,384
Don’t ever come back here again.

147
00:16:28,385 --> 00:16:30,385
And what if I do come back?

148
00:16:56,745 --> 00:16:57,745
Vin.

149
00:16:58,665 --> 00:17:00,264
Soon the government will allow people to-

150
00:17:00,265 --> 00:17:01,945
-leave the forest without prosecution.

151
00:17:04,145 --> 00:17:06,744
I’ve been ordered to prepare a reception point at the military camp.

152
00:17:06,745 --> 00:17:08,784
If you want to go home and see Aunt Laor,

153
00:17:08,785 --> 00:17:09,984
You can come anytime.

154
00:17:09,985 --> 00:17:11,344
Vin’s not going anywhere with you.

155
00:17:11,345 --> 00:17:12,945
How do you know he won’t?

156
00:17:15,585 --> 00:17:17,305
I heard that the base are a mess too.

157
00:17:18,825 --> 00:17:20,544
The government wants to help those who fled to the forest.

158
00:17:20,545 --> 00:17:22,105
Why don't you grab a chance?

159
00:17:28,025 --> 00:17:29,985
Or are you going to wait until Vin dies here too?

160
00:18:20,625 --> 00:18:22,505
Your stomach acting up again, Comrade Gaun Hin?

161
00:18:28,345 --> 00:18:29,345
Yeah.

162
00:18:29,465 --> 00:18:31,105
Do you have any medicine left?

163
00:18:33,345 --> 00:18:36,024
Comrade, Once you’re done packing, go get some rest.

164
00:18:36,025 --> 00:18:37,664
I'll take care here.

165
00:18:37,665 --> 00:18:38,945
Okay.

166
00:18:45,225 --> 00:18:46,225
What is it?

167
00:18:46,745 --> 00:18:48,025
Why did you ask to meet now?

168
00:18:48,745 --> 00:18:50,184
Do you know where Comrade Saeng went?

169
00:18:50,185 --> 00:18:51,905
We’ve looked everywhere and can’t find him.

170
00:18:52,865 --> 00:18:53,865
Umm...

171
00:18:54,145 --> 00:18:55,745
I haven’t seen him since after dinner.

172
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,225
Maybe he went on a mission.

173
00:19:04,425 --> 00:19:06,185
I found a way out of here.

174
00:19:07,225 --> 00:19:09,065
I'll take Comrade Baitong out of here.

175
00:19:10,345 --> 00:19:11,545
Come with us, please.

176
00:19:12,545 --> 00:19:13,625
Why do you want to escape?

177
00:19:20,305 --> 00:19:21,985
Have you forgotten what we stood for?

178
00:19:27,905 --> 00:19:29,225
Before we entered the forest,

179
00:19:30,825 --> 00:19:32,465
We gave up everything.

180
00:19:33,585 --> 00:19:34,705
Because we believed-

181
00:19:35,145 --> 00:19:37,345
This was the only way to make the country better.

182
00:19:38,265 --> 00:19:40,065
But ever since Comrade Fah became the leader,

183
00:19:40,745 --> 00:19:42,184
We can’t even live here in peace.

184
00:19:42,185 --> 00:19:43,384
Can't you see, Comrade?

185
00:19:43,385 --> 00:19:45,465
How is the country supposed to get better like this?

186
00:19:46,665 --> 00:19:48,545
I agree with you on Comrade Fah.

187
00:19:50,345 --> 00:19:51,545
But about escaping...

188
00:19:53,145 --> 00:19:55,505
Even if we find Comrade Saeng, he won’t go with us.

189
00:20:03,145 --> 00:20:04,825
Have you really thought this through?

190
00:20:14,225 --> 00:20:15,705
Yes, I have.

191
00:20:18,665 --> 00:20:19,665
Then...

192
00:20:22,385 --> 00:20:23,585
good luck.

193
00:20:29,985 --> 00:20:32,105
I hope one day we’ll meet again outside.

194
00:20:56,305 --> 00:20:58,824
We’ll use the supply route to leave.

195
00:20:58,825 --> 00:21:00,424
There won’t be any guards tonight.

196
00:21:00,425 --> 00:21:01,705
Don't worry.

197
00:21:02,905 --> 00:21:04,545
What about Comrade Saeng?

198
00:21:08,585 --> 00:21:09,665
Only three of us are going.

199
00:21:10,865 --> 00:21:13,305
Will we ever see Comrade Saeng again?

200
00:21:15,985 --> 00:21:16,985
Of course.

201
00:21:17,545 --> 00:21:19,144
We definitely will.

202
00:21:19,145 --> 00:21:20,225
It's only a matter of time.

203
00:21:20,865 --> 00:21:22,145
Come on. We should get moving.

204
00:21:36,825 --> 00:21:37,825
I'm sorry.

205
00:21:38,185 --> 00:21:39,344
I went to see him.

206
00:21:39,345 --> 00:21:40,625
You did it knowing it was wrong.

207
00:21:41,185 --> 00:21:42,545
Do you know how risky it was?

208
00:21:43,225 --> 00:21:45,465
What did you think when that soldier asked you to leave?

209
00:21:45,985 --> 00:21:47,465
Our base is not a good place anymore.

210
00:21:47,665 --> 00:21:48,865
The government has toned down.

211
00:21:50,305 --> 00:21:51,345
So I hesitated.

212
00:21:51,945 --> 00:21:52,945
What about me?

213
00:22:02,305 --> 00:22:03,425
Sin.

214
00:22:05,065 --> 00:22:06,465
Do you want to leave with me?

215
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:10,185
I can't leave.

216
00:22:11,545 --> 00:22:13,385
I have to stay here and take care everyone.

217
00:22:14,945 --> 00:22:16,345
They helped me when I escaped.

218
00:22:18,865 --> 00:22:20,624
If you want me to leave everyone here,

219
00:22:20,625 --> 00:22:21,625
I can't do that.

220
00:22:22,945 --> 00:22:24,465
This place already feels like my home.

221
00:22:29,545 --> 00:22:30,545
Sin.

222
00:22:31,865 --> 00:22:33,025
I mean...

223
00:22:34,105 --> 00:22:36,105
Deep within your heart,

224
00:22:37,545 --> 00:22:38,785
Do you want to leave with me?

225
00:22:45,585 --> 00:22:46,625
There's something...

226
00:22:47,985 --> 00:22:49,105
I want you to know.

227
00:23:01,025 --> 00:23:02,264
Feels like someone’s following us.

228
00:23:02,265 --> 00:23:03,265
Go. Hurry.

229
00:23:12,665 --> 00:23:13,945
Comrade Yue.

230
00:23:15,065 --> 00:23:16,344
What are you doing here?

231
00:23:16,345 --> 00:23:17,625
Why didn’t you intercept Yaguar?

232
00:23:18,225 --> 00:23:19,664
Where have Comrade Saeng been?

233
00:23:19,665 --> 00:23:21,105
He came with me.

234
00:23:34,345 --> 00:23:35,464
Comrade Yue-

235
00:23:35,465 --> 00:23:36,945
-loves Comrade Saeng.

236
00:23:37,985 --> 00:23:39,385
Isn't that right?

237
00:23:40,465 --> 00:23:41,465
Yes.

238
00:23:48,145 --> 00:23:49,905
But Comrade Saeng is a man.

239
00:23:50,625 --> 00:23:52,505
Whether he's man or woman,

240
00:23:53,745 --> 00:23:55,065
doesn't matter to me.

241
00:24:03,545 --> 00:24:04,545
Hurry!

242
00:24:15,545 --> 00:24:16,545
Hurry! Run!

243
00:24:17,905 --> 00:24:18,905
Bai Tong!

244
00:24:23,105 --> 00:24:24,105
Bai Tong!

245
00:24:24,425 --> 00:24:25,425
Are you okay?

246
00:24:26,025 --> 00:24:27,025
Climb on my back.

247
00:24:38,625 --> 00:24:40,145
Hey!

248
00:24:43,465 --> 00:24:44,465
Bai Tong.

249
00:25:01,305 --> 00:25:03,464
Comrade, didn’t we agree-

250
00:25:03,465 --> 00:25:05,625
-to send them to the main base?

251
00:25:08,105 --> 00:25:09,425
I’ll lure them over there.

252
00:25:32,785 --> 00:25:33,785
Comrade!

253
00:25:34,305 --> 00:25:35,825
I said stop shooting.

254
00:25:36,225 --> 00:25:37,464
If we kill them now,

255
00:25:37,465 --> 00:25:39,265
How will we know where the others are hiding?

256
00:25:48,425 --> 00:25:50,504
Shit! You talk too much!

257
00:25:50,505 --> 00:25:52,465
You really butt into my business.

258
00:25:57,625 --> 00:25:59,025
Bai Tong. Bai Tong.

259
00:25:59,985 --> 00:26:00,985
Bai Tong.

260
00:26:33,905 --> 00:26:35,784
Stop crying,

261
00:26:35,785 --> 00:26:37,265
get up.

262
00:26:44,465 --> 00:26:45,545
So beautiful.

263
00:26:46,625 --> 00:26:49,985
Of course. Comrade Ying made it for you.

264
00:26:50,945 --> 00:26:53,265
Comrade Ploeng has never gone anywhere far.

265
00:26:53,945 --> 00:26:55,584
He's just change a place to live.

266
00:26:55,585 --> 00:26:58,225
Now he's living in Comrade Bai Tong's heart.

267
00:26:59,265 --> 00:27:00,665
And you still have us.

268
00:27:01,225 --> 00:27:04,305
Comrade Saeng, and all comrades are still by your side.

269
00:27:28,385 --> 00:27:29,865
- Bai Tong.
- Comrade Ying.

270
00:27:30,465 --> 00:27:32,145
Go. Run. Go!

271
00:27:37,025 --> 00:27:38,265
Bai Tong.

272
00:27:44,065 --> 00:27:45,265
Bai Tong.

273
00:27:48,065 --> 00:27:49,265
Bai Tong.

274
00:27:52,185 --> 00:27:53,664
What the hell are you doing?

